An ESP32-based weather station must operate on battery power for six months without maintenance. What hardware and software modifications 
would you make to maximize battery life? 
Ans – To make the battery last for six months, I would use Deep Sleep mode so the ESP32 wakes up only when needed. I would also use low-power
sensors, disable Bluetooth, turn on Wi-Fi only while sending data, and use a high-capacity battery with an efficient voltage regulator. 
These changes reduce power consumption and increase battery life. 
